# .easignore — what EAS Build leaves OUT of the uploaded project.
#
# Why this file exists:
#   `google-services.json` is gitignored (it is a credential-ish file we do not
#   want in the repo), but app.json points `android.googleServicesFile` at it.
#   EAS uploads the project using the ignore rules, so with only .gitignore the
#   file never reaches the builder — the build either fails on the missing path
#   or, worse, succeeds with Android push silently dead. That failure is called
#   out in DONE-push-setup.md step 6.
#
# IMPORTANT: when .easignore is present, EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, not
# in addition to it. So this must stay a full mirror of .gitignore, minus only
# the Firebase client configs below. If you add a rule to .gitignore, add it
# here too — otherwise that path starts getting uploaded.
#
# Deliberately still excluded: every real secret (service-account keys,
# keystores, provisioning profiles, .env.local). Those must never leave the
# machine. Firebase *client* config is different — it ships inside the APK by
# design, so uploading it to the builder gives nothing away.

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
# NOTE: google-services.json and GoogleService-Info.plist are intentionally NOT
# listed here — they must reach the builder. Everything else stays out.
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Google service-account keys (FCM V1 / Play Store) — never upload
*-service-account*.json
tokenwalla-*.json

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

app-example

# Generated native folders. These MUST stay excluded: they exist locally (ios/
# carries a full Pods tree) and uploading them would both bloat the archive and
# push EAS into a bare-workflow build that skips prebuild and the config plugins.
/ios
/android

# Claude Code local config
.claude/

# Play publisher service account key — never ship to build workers
play-service-account.json
